---
import NerdBox from "@/components/caira/NerdBox.astro";
---

<div class="reveal">
  <div class="fig">
    <svg
      viewBox="0 0 420 300"
      role="img"
      aria-label="Loop diagram: perceive, think, act and check arranged in a circle and joined by curved arrows, with a small LLM box inside think showing the model is one small part of the loop"
    >
      <defs>
        <marker
          id="h-ar"
          markerWidth="8"
          markerHeight="8"
          refX="6.5"
          refY="3.5"
          orient="auto"
        >
          <path d="M0,0 L7,3.5 L0,7 z" style="fill:var(--cx-faint)"></path>
        </marker>
        <style is:inline>
          .hcirc {
            fill: var(--cx-ink3);
            stroke: var(--cx-teal);
            stroke-width: 1.8;
          }
          .hlbl {
            font-family: var(--cx-mono);
            font-size: 12px;
            font-weight: 700;
            fill: var(--cx-text);
            text-anchor: middle;
          }
          .hsub {
            font-family: var(--cx-mono);
            font-size: 9.5px;
            fill: var(--cx-muted);
            text-anchor: middle;
          }
          .harc {
            stroke: var(--cx-faint);
            stroke-width: 1.8;
            fill: none;
            marker-end: url(#h-ar);
          }
          .hchip {
            fill: var(--cx-ink4);
            stroke: var(--cx-amber);
            stroke-width: 1.3;
          }
          .hchipt {
            font-family: var(--cx-mono);
            font-size: 8.5px;
            font-weight: 700;
            fill: var(--cx-amber);
            text-anchor: middle;
          }
        </style>
      </defs>

      <circle class="hcirc" cx="210" cy="60" r="44"></circle>
      <text class="hlbl" x="210" y="57">PERCEIVE</text>
      <text class="hsub" x="210" y="73">read what arrived</text>

      <circle class="hcirc" cx="350" cy="150" r="44"></circle>
      <text class="hlbl" x="350" y="141">THINK</text>
      <text class="hsub" x="350" y="156">decide what's needed</text>
      <rect class="hchip" x="324" y="164" width="52" height="18" rx="4"></rect>
      <text class="hchipt" x="350" y="176">LLM</text>

      <circle class="hcirc" cx="210" cy="242" r="44"></circle>
      <text class="hlbl" x="210" y="239">ACT</text>
      <text class="hsub" x="210" y="255">do it</text>

      <circle class="hcirc" cx="70" cy="150" r="44"></circle>
      <text class="hlbl" x="70" y="147">CHECK</text>
      <text class="hsub" x="70" y="163">confirm it worked</text>

      <path class="harc flow-dash" d="M 248 82 Q 320 100 340 108"></path>
      <path class="harc flow-dash" d="M 330 188 Q 290 225 252 236"></path>
      <path class="harc flow-dash" d="M 168 230 Q 100 210 82 192"></path>
      <path class="harc flow-dash" d="M 82 110 Q 120 80 168 68"></path>
    </svg>
    <div class="figcap">
      The whole trick of AI engineering: everyone gets the same models. The
      harness is where products differ.
    </div>
  </div>

  <NerdBox title="the loop, in real code">
    <p>
      One function IS the loop: resolve tenant, detect intent, run the matched
      flow, and persist state only after a successful send. That last detail is
      a check most builders forget. Not a single vendor import inside it: every
      dependency arrives through a port, and the LLM is called from exactly one
      narrow place inside think.
    </p>
  </NerdBox>
</div>
